Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I've discretized my polygon data to the proximity detector type. Is there a way to get the new xy coordinates for the discretized capture history?

Using xy(capture_history) works for a non-discretized capture history created using read.capthist(), but this doesn't work on discretized capture histories, because the new capture history no longer has the xy coordinates, only TrapID. How can I get the spatial locations of the TrapID's?

Thank you

From u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com  Wed Jan 16 02:08:17 2019
From: u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com (Murray Efford)
Date: Wed, 16 Jan 2019 02:08:17 +0000
Subject: Re: Trap coordinates from discretize()
Message-ID: <1HuiaoehvIk.0OTkVLBiCAAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <1HuiaoehvIk.okQJqM5ZCAAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
References: <1HuiaoehvIk.okQJqM5ZCAAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/secrgroup/c/1HuiaoehvIk/m/0OTkVLBiCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I think traps(CH1)[trap(CH1),] should do it. For example, extending the example for discretize:

library(secr)
pol <- make.poly()
CH <- sim.capthist(pol, popn = list(D = 30), detectpar = list(g0 = 0.3))
CH1 <- discretize(CH, spacing = 10, output = 'count')
cbind(animalID(CH1), occasion(CH1), traps(CH1)[trap(CH1),])

See also the plot at the end of Examples.

Murray

