Subject: More than one detection per occasion in sim.capthist
Message-ID: <KauQ_zG0K9A.O8-ABrMDFgAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/secrgroup/c/KauQ_zG0K9A/m/O8-ABrMDFgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'm attempting to run sim.popn and sim.capthist together to create simulated capture histories. However I'm having trouble getting more than one detection of an individual per occasion.

Here is my code:

caps <- read.capthist('data.txt', 'perimeter_LS.txt', fmt = 'XY', detector = 'polygon')

tpop.sexF = sim.popn(D = 0.0003, popn = caps, core = traps, buffer = 17000, model2D = "cluster", buffertype = "rect", poly = data.shape, details = list(mu = 10, hsigma = 1), Ndist = "fixed", covariates = list(sex = c(F = 1.0, M = 0.0)))

tpop.sexF.df <- as.data.frame(tpop.sexF)
trapsF <- read.traps(data = tpop.sexF.df)

tch.F = sim.capthist(trapsF, tpop.sexF, detectfn = 'HEX', detectpar = list(g0 = 0.16, sigma = 2600), noccasions = 3, binomN = 10)

inds <- tch.F.df %>%
  group_by(ID, Occasion) %>%
  tally() %>%
  mutate(n = as.numeric(n))
summary(inds$n)
##    Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.
##       1       1       1       1       1       1
I created trapsF so that sim.capthist would use the detection locations in sim.popn instead of creating new locations - this always gave me too many locations (I am attempting simulate detections at around 60-80 locations, it was producing a couple hundred).

When I check the number of individuals per occasions, I'm only getting one, which isn't what I want. I thought setting binomN would change the number of detections, or even Ndist, but I've been changing several variables and I'm not getting anything different.

Anyone have any suggestions about what I'm missing?

Thanks

