't' is a factor, so needs to be presented as such in newdata. Also you seem to have omitted 'g'.
It's easier to just use predict(fit.t, all.levels = TRUE) (documentation hidden in ?secr.make.newdata).
This worked for me:

library(secr)
mask <- make.mask(traps(ovenCH), buffer = 300, nx = 25)
fit.t<- secr.fit(ovenCH, model = list(D ~ Session, g0~t, sigma~g), groups="Sex",
    mask = mask, trace = T,  verify = F, detectfn = 2)
## There were mostly 10 occasions per session in the ovenbird mistnetting
predict(fit.t, newdata = expand.grid(Session = 0, t = factor(1:3, levels=1:10), g = c('F','M')) )
## or just
predict(fit.t, all.levels=TRUE)

