The mask needs to be large enough that it includes every animal that might be detected, even if it is at risk for only one primary session. You can get that by running ch <- join() to create a pooled capthist object and then running mask <- make.mask(traps(ch), buffer = xxx, nx = yyy, type = 'trapbuffer') where xxx is appropriate to lynx and yyy is some number >= 32 (determines the coarseness of the mask). The result may still be crazy - you will have to see!

