Hello, I have been using the secr package for some time and just recently have been fitting nonspatial models using openCR. Because I have formatted my data for secr models in the past, I have been using that capthist data format for openCR as well. I have noticed that varying the trap usage in the capthist does not have any effect on the nonspatial model results. I understand that the spatial component does not matter, but I would think that the total sample effort would still be important. My main question is whether or not there is a way to incorporate varied sampling effort between occasions into openCR? Accompanying question: is my thinking on this is wrong and it is not in fact important to consider this when the spatial component is removed?

